              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zháoliáng — \"to catch a chill\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zuótiān wǒ zháoliáng le — I caught a chill yesterday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zháoliáng is built from zháo 'to be touched by' and liáng 'cool', both inherited from Middle Chinese, drjak and ljang (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to attach to' and the second 'thin' and 'cold'."
            }
          ]
        },
